      "math_academy_id": "q-140568",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{140}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{35}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{35}})≈{75.31}^{∘}.\n$$",
